 "intro_zh": "华山古称“西岳”，雅称“太华山”，中国五岳之一。华山雄伟奇峻，山势峻峭，壁立千仞，群峰挺秀，自古以来就有“华山天下险”“奇险天下第一山”美誉。",
 "intro_en": "Mount Hua (simplified Chinese: 华山; traditional Chinese: 華山; pinyin: Huà Shān) is a mountain located near the city of Huayin in Shaanxi Province, about 120 kilometres (75 mi) east of Xi'an. It is the \"Western Mountain\" of the Five Great Mountains of China and has a long history of religious significance. Originally classified as having three peaks, in modern times it is classified as having five main peaks, the highest of which is the South Peak at 2,154.9 metres (7,070 ft).",
 "intro_en_source": "wikipedia",
